  "question": {
    "text": "What will be current through the $200 \\Omega$\r\nresistor in the given circuit, a long time after the switch $K$ is made on?\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2018_phy_q2.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "v0wED",
      "text": "Zero",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DBSDx",
      "text": "$100 \\mathrm{mA}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Jv5RK",
      "text": "$10 \\mathrm{mA}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IKrfM",
      "text": "$1 \\mathrm{mA}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In steady state, arm having capacitors does not flow current. So, we can neglect them.\r\n$\\therefore$ The given circuit reduces to\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2018_phy_a2.png\">\r\n\r\n$$\r\nR_{\\text {net }}=200+400=600 \\Omega\r\n$$\r\n$\\therefore$ Current in circuit,\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\nI=\\frac{V}{R} &=\\frac{6}{600}=0.01 \\mathrm{A} \\\\\r\n&=10 \\mathrm{mA}\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
